# the keys from MIDI in (midicc.c key_midi). Step record: REC tapped while stopped arms it; a note over MIDI for the track on
# the screen (its channel, or 12 to 16) writes the cursor step as the FM-1's keys do, notes held together make a
# chord, the first note's velocity is the step's; another track's channel writes nothing; the mode off, nothing
wait 300
turn ALGO 1
expect trk 2
tap REC
wait 60
# C4 on channel 2 (T2), velocity 100: step 1
midi 91 3C 64
wait 20
midi 81 3C 40
wait 60
expect note 2 1 1 60
expect stepvel 2 1 1 100
# a note-on with velocity 0 is the off; velocity 80 kept
midi 91 40 50
wait 20
midi 91 40 00
wait 60
expect note 2 1 2 64
expect stepvel 2 1 2 80
# a chord: three notes held together land on step 3; the cursor moves only once they are all up
midi 91 3C 64
midi 91 40 64
midi 91 43 64
wait 30
midi 81 3C 00
midi 81 40 00
wait 30
expect note 2 1 4 0
midi 81 43 00
wait 60
expect note 2 1 3 60
expect noteat 2 1 3 2 64
expect noteat 2 1 3 3 67
expect noteat 2 1 3 4 0
# channel 12: the track selected
midi 9B 45 64
wait 20
midi 8B 45 00
wait 60
expect note 2 1 4 69
# channel 3 is T3, not the track on the screen: nothing written, and its off moves nothing
midi 92 47 64
wait 20
midi 82 47 00
wait 60
expect note 2 1 5 0
# an off for a note that was never counted moves nothing either
midi 81 30 00
wait 60
expect note 2 1 5 0
# REC tapped again: the mode off; a note plays but writes nothing
tap REC
wait 60
midi 91 3C 64
wait 20
midi 81 3C 00
wait 60
expect note 2 1 5 0
# the notes a step writes: no SEQ needed for MIDI; E4 G4 played on the track's channel, let go, then a step tapped
# (white key w5, step 6, empty) gets them
midi 91 40 64
midi 91 43 64
wait 30
midi 81 40 00
midi 81 43 00
wait 60
tapkey w5
wait 60
expect note 2 1 6 64
expect noteat 2 1 6 2 67
expect noteat 2 1 6 3 0
# chord mode (chordmode.xy's way in: a step held, SEQ tapped): a chord over MIDI writes the held step's notes, its
# length stays; a note on another channel writes nothing; SEQ again ends it
notes 2 1 8 4 100 60
expect slen 2 8 16
key w7 down
wait 30
tap SEQ
wait 30
key w7 up
wait 30
midi 91 3E 64
midi 91 41 64
wait 30
midi 81 3E 00
midi 81 41 00
wait 60
expect note 2 1 8 62
expect noteat 2 1 8 2 65
expect slen 2 8 16
midi 92 47 64
wait 20
midi 82 47 00
wait 60
expect note 2 1 8 62
tap SEQ
wait 60
# chord mode off: a MIDI note is the memory again, not step 8
midi 91 48 64
wait 20
midi 81 48 00
wait 60
expect note 2 1 8 62
tapkey w8
wait 60
expect note 2 1 9 72
